# THE WARDS' PIECES ON A WALL (StructureSystem::updateWardLooks). Written by hand. Every piece is modelled for the +X
# side of a 2 m wall segment, in the WALL's space: its origin (1.5 m over the ground), the ground at y = -1.5, the wall's
# side at x = 1, the cell's edges at z = -1 and z = 1. The game turns each piece about +Y to the other sides.
#   ResistPane   - the barrier: a full-size pane of light in front of the side (x 1.06 .. 1.16), the cell's whole width
#                  (two segments' panes meet edge to edge) and the wall's height and a bit more (to 3.25 m).
#   ResistCorner - the post at the OUTER corner of two panes (+X and +Z), so the barrier goes round a corner with no seam.
#   AbsorbPane   - a smaller pane in front of the barrier (x 1.28 .. 1.34): it does not touch the ResistPane.
#   Spikes       - five cones of light out of the wall's side, through both panes (to x = 1.8).
# The boxes: 8 positions a piece, the faces name them RELATIVE (-8 .. -1), and they share one UV and the six normals
# 1 +X  2 -X  3 +Y  4 -Y  5 +Z  6 -Z. The cones: 8 sides, one normal per side (7 .. 14), no base (it is in the wall).
